.TH wait_pid_nohang 3 "2025" "lib" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
wait_pid_nohang \- wait for a specific child process to exit

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "wait.h"
.PP
.BI "int wait_pid_nohang(int " pid ", int* " wstat ");"

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wait_pid_nohang
function waits for the child process identified by
.IR pid 
to terminate.

.SH BEHAVIOR
.SS Unix
On Unix-like systems, this function repeatedly calls
.BR wait_nohang (2)
to reap terminated child processes until the process with the specified
.I pid
is found. If
.B wait_nohang
returns 0 (no children have exited) or -1 (error), the function returns that value immediately, without blocking for the specific
.IR pid .
The exit status of the reaped process is stored in the integer pointed to by
.IR wstat .

.SS Windows
On Windows, the current implementation uses
.BR WaitForSingleObject (3)
with an infinite timeout. Note that despite the "nohang" suffix, the Windows implementation will block until the specified process terminates.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the
.I pid
of the terminated process upon success. 
Returns 0 if no status is currently available (Unix only).
Returns -1 if the process does not exist or an error occurs.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wait_nohang (3),
.BR wait_pid (3)